# =============================================================================
# SUMMARY, DERIVED FROM THE SIX RUNS ABOVE AND FROM NOTHING ELSE
# =============================================================================
#
# ZEROED GROUP AGAINST THE TOTAL FILL, encode, min .. max over six runs
#
# payload  what it is                 ns per element        zeroed/total
# P1.2     M1, every field present    -1.66 ..  +1.70       0.986 .. 1.014
# P1.3     M1, the absent path        -4.98 ..  -4.06       0.719 .. 0.766
# P2.2     M2, the deciding shape    -26.18 .. -13.02       0.970 .. 0.985
# P2.5     M2, the absent path        -0.42 ..  +0.17       0.983 .. 1.007
#
#   Negative is a saving. The threshold to judge the cost against is the 5.4 ns per
#   ResultRaw and 24.4 per TaskDetailed that ABI v1 section 6 prices the CODEC-side reset
#   at; the worst cost measured here is +1.70 ns per element.
#
# RATIO TO PROST, min .. max over six runs, encode
#
# payload  arm                 / prost
# P1.2     core-ffi-rust       0.690 .. 0.710
# P1.2     core-ffi-zeroed     0.681 .. 0.720
# P1.3     core-ffi-rust       1.108 .. 1.188      <- the absent-path inversion
# P1.3     core-ffi-zeroed     0.815 .. 0.857      <- gone
# P2.2     core-ffi-rust       0.776 .. 0.795
# P2.2     core-ffi-zeroed     0.764 .. 0.774
# P2.5     core-ffi-rust       0.728 .. 0.748
# P2.5     core-ffi-zeroed     0.716 .. 0.736
#
# CORRECTNESS
#   Byte identity against the validated manifest on ALL EIGHT M1/M2 payloads plus P3.1,
#   under both the total fill and the zeroed group, in every run. P3.1 is in the list
#   because explicit presence and the oneof are where a sparse fill can be WRONG rather
#   than merely slow, and positive control 3 shows that row does its job.
#
# WHAT IS NOT MEASURED
#   - Decode. There is no host-side group fill on decode to change.
#   - The nested groups inside an element: only the top-level element group is zeroed.
#   - M4 to M7. The generator emits the variant for every root, so the arms exist; only
#     M1, M2 and M3 are exercised here.
#   - What this costs a host that is not Rust. The proposal replaces an unconditional store
#     per field with a branch per field, and what a branch costs is a property of the host.
#   - Whether the ABI SHOULD change. This is an arm and a set of numbers; the contract
#     change and its cost to every other binding are not this slice's to weigh.
